    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for google-osconfig-agent",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for google-osconfig-agent fixes the following issues:\n\n- CVE-2026-41178: go.opentelemetry.io/otel/baggage: no rejection of raw-length headers in baggage parsing allows for DoS\n  via oversized inputs (bsc#1276722).\n- CVE-2026-56854,CVE-2026-56855,CVE-2026-78662: golang.org/x/crypto/ssh: authentication bypass and deadlocks in the\n  crypto/ssh library (bsc#1278597).\n\nChanges for google-osconfig-agent:\n\n- Update to version 20260911.00\n * Add support for all possible SCALIBR os extractor for linux (#1052)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
